            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0552" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5155: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-24T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                                1927—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>346. The aeroplanes yesterday for the first time definitely located Sandino’s
                    stronghold at Chipote. They bombed a storehouse there killing at least four
                    bandits. Both planes were hit by bullets.</p>
                <p>This discovery is very important as it now should be possible to make a decisive
                    attack on Sandino as soon as adequate preparations can be made. The nature of
                    the surrounding country makes military operations extremely difficult.</p>
                <p>Information has been received indicating that 600 Honduraneans have joined
                    Sandino in the last few months.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
